desc:
Hi ! Slaps... Beans... what do you need more ?
@sebastiendelf and myself are bringing to you a fun table based on these 2 heroes' movies.  Don't forget to check out Sébastion other works like Spawn or Megaman tables.
This table is a mod from original IT Pinball Madness table so thanks to :
 JPSalas for his permission to mod the table
@JoePicasso for his permission to mod the table
Pedro Pires from @TeamTuga for his permission to mod the pup-pack.
@floeschng and @yid4lyf for Deutch and English pup-packs.
@DarrinVPCLE for adding some nice LED DOF effects (don't forget to update your DOF Files)
@IgaBiva @Panasony for their precious help adding VR-ROOM, I'm sure VR is the next big thing for Virtual Pinball...
@Ext2k for his permission to use his VR Room model
@Smaug for his premiere on GameClubCentral
Beta-testers....

I wish I could propose pup-pack in Italian. .... Cause everybody loves these 2 guys !!!

11 Missions, 11 Movies, 11 Villains to fight, 4 Multiball modes, 3 Wizards modes : I can tell you it'll be a lot of fun !

R.I.P. Bud Spencer...

@Sebastony helpfully added that this is a re-theme of the layout for Congo (Williams, 1995). The ROM interface has evidently been removed, but not yet replaced with native table rules.

- To be clear, this seems to be demo-only at this point. You can launch a ball and use flippers, and get a sense of how the game plays, but that's it.

- I'm thinking spookymoulder is in fact the same person as @theGhost787. The table info seems to suggest that, anyway. Point is-- Ghost seemed to intend most (or all?) of his VP projects to be starters, meant for others to complete. Therefore, I figure this table would probably make for excellent mod material.

@bombaj344 and @BurtMacklin  Present to you a reskin MOD of the Elektra table originally made by 32assassin and francisco666  and later modded by @bigus1.  Huge thanks to everyone that was involved in the original table creation.

@bombaj344 did amazing work on the artwork on this table to really show off Dr. Jekyll and Mr Hyde.  @bombaj344 reached out to me for help with this table and to share it with the community.
I made some script adds for the sounds and created arts and B2S files.  For example the ROM sounds of the original table will mute at table launch and will enable again for that rom after the table exit.
Thanks to @HiRez00 for his wonderful music scripts also that are used in this table.

Included in the zip is a 2 screen B2s, 3 screen B2S, Table, Music, FullDMD video, Topper video and wheel arts for your front end.
This is my first table upload and first to work with @bombaj344, I hope everyone enjoys!

THANKS:
JP Salas allowed me to use his Attack From Mars table as a base and provided advice during the creation.
@KRAKEN provided the original Attack From Mars Serum colorization, which was an immense help and saved me countless hours of dumping, masking and assigning frames. He also fixed many bugs in the video mode I would have never figured out on my own.
@apophis invited me to the VPW Discord and kindly let us use his asteroid for the VR room.
@DGrimmReaper created an awesome VR room, just looks so insanely good.
@cyberpez let me use key assets of his AFM table, which made the table so so much better.
@Thalamus supportive on VPU since day one and connected me to the VPW team.
@r2z2 and RomKnight provided insight on using Claude for VPX code optimization.
@hauntfreaks 's backglass was a template for the modded b2s.

ASSUMING DIRECT CONTROL

Modded Attack From Mars with more than 1500 callouts from the Mass Effect trilogy + more than 60 music tracks + effects, textures and 3d models from the games.
Full playfield, backglass, sound and DMD (Serum) reskin with nfozzy physics and fleep sounds, Flupper bumpers, rothbauerw flashers. Crank up the volume and dive into the frantic soundscape ;)

This table includes a few "enchanced" gameplay elements inspired by the games, some of them are physics-altering in a non-realistic way. They can all be toggled in F12 menu or live by hitting both magna-save keys.
Enhancements include:
- Biotic powers (Stasis, Throw, Pull, Barrier) cycle with left magnasave, activate with right magnasave. (new power becomes available after each beaten wave.)
- Mass relay jump when completing a full orbit
- Reaper cannon shots on ball in vision cone during attack waves.
- Kickbacks, recharged by collecting Paragon (left ramp/orbit shots) and Renegade points (right ramp/orbit shots)
- Flipper strength ramp-up during Suicide Mission: each second passed and each jackpot hit in Suicide Mission (Total Annihilation) will increase the flipper strength.
- Ball manipulation during Indoctrination: Balls velocity remote controlled during this MB.
- Auto aim during Normandy MB: balls in the center area are automatically launched into the center target. Deactivated by default as it makes jackpot shots difficult
